window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-9356628262df0852"]={"key":"ny_b1-9356628262df0852","group":"ny_b1","uid":"9356628262df0852","rank":87,"title":"tessington archive vendor capability comparison","occupation":"audio_video_technicians","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are Callum Fontaine, the audio and video technician at Tessington Heritage Archive, and archivist Ilse Baranowski needs your procurement-panel pack by 20 September 2025. The archive has grant funding to digitise 1,400 obsolete-format tapes this quarter, covering U-matic, 1/4-inch open reel at two speeds, and DAT, and we need to appoint a service bureau rather than attempt the work in-house. Use the attached `vendor_evidence_packet.xlsx` as the evidence available to you: it contains the supplier material and dated notes gathered for this decision, and you must not use live web research or fill gaps with assumptions. Prepare `digitisation_vendor_comparison.xlsx` and `digitisation_vendor_recommendation.docx` in the top level of the working directory, using exactly those filenames. Please make the workbook the auditable comparison table for every credible bureau that can actually handle the collection, including the relevant format and speed capability, evidence date and strength, current rate basis, estimated collection cost, stated or calculated turnaround, output and handover specifications, material limitations, and unresolved questions or risks. Distinguish a capability that is supported by current operational evidence from an advertisement, an old case study, or a statement that cannot be verified; the panel needs to see both credible inclusions and credible exclusions, not a list of marketing claims. Where the packet contains a published price sheet and a conflicting quotation, show the figures and the comparison basis rather than silently choosing one, and make clear which figure is used in any estimate. Treat the 2023 case study naming equipment later reported as sold with the care appropriate to a procurement decision. Ilse has already promised the panel that the shortlist will include every bureau advertising all three formats, but that promise sits uneasily with our obligation not to present a bureau as capable when the evidence does not support current access to the necessary transports. We also cannot obtain test transfers or fresh written confirmations from every candidate before the panel meets, so use a defensible fallback for that time constraint and expose its limits. The accompanying Word document is for the panel, not for an engineer: keep it to two pages maximum, state one and only one recommended bureau, explain the decision against capability, cost, timing, deliverables, and evidence confidence, and identify the principal fallback or risk without turning the ending into a list of next steps. Anchor the recommendation in the workbook's figures, including the 1,400-tape scope and the estimated total cost and turnaround, and ensure the same figures agree wherever they appear in both files. Apply the procurement context of England as at 30 June 2025, label evidence dates clearly, preserve source distinctions, and do not invent current rates, equipment, capacity, insurance, accreditation, or contractual terms that the packet does not establish. The grant-funded collection must be treated as one decision while still showing where format mix, speed, or output requirements affect feasibility. Use readable professional presentation, make calculations traceable, and leave the panel able to understand what is known, what is merely claimed, and why your single recommendation is defensible by the deadline.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/vendor_evidence_packet.xlsx` — The sole offline evidence source for supplier identities, format and speed claims, dated operational confirmations, published prices, conflicting quote information, equipment-status notes, turnaround statements, and deliverable specifications.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `digitisation_vendor_comparison.xlsx` — An auditable comparison of all credible candidate bureaus and the evidence-supported reasons for inclusion or exclusion. (Must be saved at the top level of the working directory with exactly this filename.; Must include traceable calculations for the 1,400-tape scope.; Must distinguish supported facts, supplier claims, conflicts, assumptions, and unresolved risks.; Must be readable without relying on hidden cells or external links.)\n- `digitisation_vendor_recommendation.docx` — A concise procurement-panel recommendation that makes one clear vendor call and explains the evidence, cost, timing, deliverables, and risk. (Must be saved at the top level of the working directory with exactly this filename.; Must be no more than two pages when rendered.; Must state exactly one recommended bureau.; Must agree with the workbook on every shared figure, especially scope, estimated total cost, and turnaround.; Must end with the decision rather than a list of next steps.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/vendor_evidence_packet.xlsx","bytes":8394,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/ae2519c604704abe447b4893c6c6e664d24546d24132bb20663c2d314e2f2508.xlsx","sha256":"ae2519c604704abe447b4893c6c6e664d24546d24132bb20663c2d314e2f2508","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Evidence packet","row_count":32,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Tessington Heritage Archive — vendor evidence packet"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Offline source snapshot; evidence assessed as at 30 June 2025. Dates are source dates, not verification dates."]},{"r":"4","cells":["Entry ID","Candidate / source","Evidence date","Source type","Format / speed","Statement or figure","Output / handover","Turnaround / capacity","Limitations / status"]},{"r":"5","cells":["E01","Thistledown Studios","2025-06-18","Dated operations email","U-matic","Current PAL/NTSC U-matic playback confirmed on in-house VO-9800 transport.","10-bit capture; ProRes proxy available.","Up to 150 tapes/week; condition dependent.","Operational confirmation; no test transfer supplied."]},{"r":"6","cells":["E02","Thistledown Studios","2025-06-18","Dated operations email","DAT","Current 44.1/48 kHz DAT playback confirmed; timecode breaks logged.","BWF WAV, 24-bit/96 kHz; cue sheet.","Up to 150 tapes/week; condition dependent.","Operational confirmation; no test transfer supplied."]},{"r":"7","cells":["E03","Thistledown Studios","2025-06-18","Dated operations email","1/4-inch open reel — 3.75 ips","Current NAB/CCIR path confirmed at 3.75 ips.","BWF WAV, 24-bit/96 kHz; leader notes.","Up to 150 tapes/week; condition dependent.","Operational confirmation; azimuth correction where possible."]},{"r":"8","cells":["E04","Thistledown Studios","2025-06-18","Dated operations email","1/4-inch open reel — 7.5 ips","Current NAB/CCIR path confirmed at 7.5 ips.","BWF WAV, 24-bit/96 kHz; leader notes.","Up to 150 tapes/week; condition dependent.","Operational confirmation; azimuth correction where possible."]},{"r":"9","cells":["E05","Thistledown Studios","2025-01-15","Published price sheet","Rates: U-matic / DAT / 3.75 / 7.5","£22 / £18 / £28 / £32 per tape.","As above; checksum manifest included.","Price sheet gives no collection turnaround.","Published rates; excludes severe mould/baking and carrier return."]},{"r":"10","cells":["E06","Thistledown Studios","2025-06-24","Quotation ref TS-0624","Rates: U-matic / DAT / 3.75 / 7.5","£24 / £19 / £30 / £35 per tape; quote valid 30 days.","BWF WAV plus 1080p H.264 access copy; CSV metadata.","10 weeks for up to 1,500 tapes from receipt; subject to condition.","Conflicts with E05; quotation is newer and scope-specific."]},{"r":"11","cells":["E07","Thornbury Health Network","2025-05-30","Supplier email","U-matic","Playback available via current partner arrangement; no serial or test file.","16-bit WAV; MP4 access copy; basic CSV.","Indicative 12 weeks for 1,400 tapes; capacity not reserved.","Current statement but partner dependency; capability partly supported."]},{"r":"12","cells":["E08","Thornbury Health Network","2025-05-30","Supplier email","DAT","44.1/48 kHz DAT transfer stated; no test file.","16-bit WAV; MP4 access copy; basic CSV.","Indicative 12 weeks for 1,400 tapes; capacity not reserved.","Current statement but partner dependency; capability partly supported."]},{"r":"13","cells":["E09","Thornbury Health Network","2025-05-30","Supplier email","1/4-inch open reel — 3.75 ips","3.75 ips transfer stated.","16-bit WAV; MP4 access copy; basic CSV.","Indicative 12 weeks for 1,400 tapes; capacity not reserved.","Current statement; 7.5 ips not addressed."]},{"r":"14","cells":["E10","Thornbury Health Network","2025-05-30","Website advertisement","1/4-inch open reel — 7.5 ips","“Reel-to-reel at multiple speeds” advertised; no dated operational confirmation.","Website says WAV/MP4; metadata unspecified.","No capacity statement.","Advertising claim only; cannot establish current 7.5 ips access."]},{"r":"15","cells":["E11","Thornbury Health Network","2025-04-02","Published price list","Rates: U-matic / DAT / 3.75 / 7.5","£20 / £16 / £26 / £30 per tape.","16-bit WAV/MP4; basic CSV.","No whole-collection commitment.","Published rates; 7.5 rate rests on advertisement."]},{"r":"16","cells":["E12","Amberline Media","2023-09-14","Case study","U-matic and 1/4-inch open reel — 7.5 ips","Case study names Sony VO-9800 and Studer A80 for a 2023 project.","24-bit WAV; ProRes; EBUCore XML in case study.","Case study says 8 weeks for 600 items.","Historical evidence only."]},{"r":"17","cells":["E13","Amberline Media","2025-02-11","Equipment-status note","Sony VO-9800","Amberline reports the named VO-9800 was sold in November 2024.","—","—","Later note weakens E12; current U-matic access unresolved."]},{"r":"18","cells":["E14","Amberline Media","2025-02-11","Equipment-status note","Studer A80","A80 retained but maintenance status not supplied; 3.75 ips not stated.","—","—","Current access to both speeds unresolved."]},{"r":"19","cells":["E15","Amberline Media","2025-06-01","Website advertisement","DAT","DAT digitisation advertised; no dated operational confirmation.","WAV/MP4 stated; metadata unspecified.","“Typical 6–10 weeks” with no batch basis.","Advertising claim only; cannot prove full collection."]},{"r":"20","cells":["E16","Fenwick Signal Bureau","2025-06-10","Dated operations email","1/4-inch open reel — 3.75 and 7.5 ips","Both speeds confirmed on current Otari MX-5050.","BWF WAV 24-bit/96 kHz; cue sheet.","8 weeks for 1,400 reels only; capacity statement is format-specific.","No U-matic or DAT transport evidence."]},{"r":"21","cells":["E17","Fenwick Signal Bureau","2025-06-10","Dated operations email","DAT","“Can source DAT deck if awarded”; no current deck identified.","BWF WAV proposed; no sample.","No whole-collection timing including DAT.","Unverified contingent claim; not current operational evidence."]},{"r":"22","cells":["E18","Fenwick Signal Bureau","2025-03-20","Published price list","Rates: 3.75 / 7.5 / DAT","£25 / £29 / £17 per tape; U-matic not listed.","BWF WAV; cue sheet.","Per-item estimates only.","Missing U-matic price/capability."]},{"r":"23","cells":["E19","Northmere Transfer Co","2025-06-12","Dated operations email","U-matic, DAT, 1/4-inch at 3.75 and 7.5 ips","All formats/speeds stated current; equipment serials not provided.","24-bit WAV; FFV1 Matroska for video; CSV manifest.","“Approx. 14 weeks” for 1,400 mixed tapes; queue dependent.","Current statement but no independent test or capacity reservation."]},{"r":"24","cells":["E20","Northmere Transfer Co","2025-05-01","Published price sheet","Rates: U-matic / DAT / 3.75 / 7.5","£21 / £17 / £27 / £31 per tape.","As above; checksum manifest.","No guaranteed completion date.","Published rates; exclusions for mould/baking."]},{"r":"27","cells":["Collection mix supplied for estimate"]},{"r":"28","cells":["Format / speed","Tape count","Basis"]},{"r":"29","cells":["U-matic","400","Scope note dated 2025-06-20"]},{"r":"30","cells":["DAT","300","Scope note dated 2025-06-20"]},{"r":"31","cells":["1/4-inch open reel — 3.75 ips","350","Scope note dated 2025-06-20"]},{"r":"32","cells":["1/4-inch open reel — 7.5 ips","350","Scope note dated 2025-06-20"]},{"r":"33","cells":["TOTAL","1400","Grant-funded collection"]},{"r":"35","cells":["E21","Archive scope note","2025-06-20","Dated archive note","Collection mix","1,400 tapes: 400 U-matic; 300 DAT; 350 open reel 3.75 ips; 350 open reel 7.5 ips.","","",""]},{"r":"37","cells":["Currency: GBP (£). Prices are per tape unless stated. No live web research used."]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/digitisation_vendor_comparison.xlsx","bytes":9070,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/1c04dedc97347d477c318545f91c73067301d36c3bd5d71bf8532de91a82ccf0.xlsx","sha256":"1c04dedc97347d477c318545f91c73067301d36c3bd5d71bf8532de91a82ccf0","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Panel comparison","row_count":17,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Tessington Heritage Archive — digitisation vendor comparison"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Decision cut-off: 30 June 2025 | Scope: 1,400 tapes | Currency: GBP (£) | Source: vendor_evidence_packet.xlsx"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Candidate","Full-format capability","U-matic evidence","DAT evidence","Open reel 3.75 ips","Open reel 7.5 ips","Evidence confidence / dates","Rate basis shown","Estimated collection cost (£)","Turnaround (scope + qualifier)","Output / handover","Material limitations / unresolved risks","Decision / source trail"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Thistledown Studios","YES — current evidence for all required formats/speeds","Supported — E01, 2025-06-18","Supported — E02, 2025-06-18","Supported — E03, 2025-06-18","Supported — E04, 2025-06-18","High: dated operations email 2025-06-18; quote 2025-06-24","Published E05 vs quote E06; estimate uses newer quote","=400*24+300*19+350*30+350*35  [缓存: 缺失]","10 weeks for up to 1,500 tapes from receipt; condition dependent (E06)","BWF WAV 24-bit/96 kHz; 1080p H.264 access copy; CSV metadata; checksum manifest","Quote £24/£19/£30/£35 conflicts with sheet £22/£18/£28/£32; no test transfer; severe mould/baking excluded","RECOMMEND — E01–E06; cost calc below"]},{"r":"6","cells":["Northmere Transfer Co","YES — current statement covers all required formats/speeds","Supported statement — E19, 2025-06-12","Supported statement — E19, 2025-06-12","Supported statement — E19, 2025-06-12","Supported statement — E19, 2025-06-12","Medium: dated email 2025-06-12; no serials/test; price E20 2025-05-01","Published E20; no quotation","=400*21+300*17+350*27+350*31  [缓存: 缺失]","Approx. 14 weeks for 1,400 mixed tapes; queue dependent (E19)","24-bit WAV; FFV1 Matroska video; CSV manifest; checksum","No capacity reservation or guaranteed date; no independent test; mould/baking exclusions","INCLUDE WITH RESERVATION — E19–E20"]},{"r":"7","cells":["Thornbury Health Network","NO — 7.5 ips is advertising only","Current/partner statement — E07, 2025-05-30","Current statement — E08, 2025-05-30","Current statement — E09, 2025-05-30","Advertising only — E10, 2025-05-30","Low/medium: 3 current statements, one advertisement; 7.5 unverified","Published E11; 7.5 rate rests on advertisement","=400*20+300*16+350*26+350*30  [缓存: 缺失]","Indicative 12 weeks for 1,400 tapes; capacity not reserved (E07–E09)","16-bit WAV; MP4; basic CSV; metadata unspecified","Partner dependency; no 7.5 operational proof; no whole-collection commitment","EXCLUDE FROM FULL-COLLECTION CAPABILITY — E07–E11"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Fenwick Signal Bureau","NO — no U-matic evidence","No evidence; E18 omits U-matic","Contingent “can source” claim — E17, 2025-06-10","Supported — E16, 2025-06-10","Supported — E16, 2025-06-10","Medium for reels; low for DAT; absent for U-matic","Published E18 for reels/DAT; no U-matic rate","=300*17+350*25+350*29  [缓存: 缺失]","8 weeks for 1,400 reels only; no mixed-collection timing (E16)","BWF WAV 24-bit/96 kHz; cue sheet","Missing U-matic transport and price; DAT deck contingent/unverified","EXCLUDE — E16–E18"]},{"r":"9","cells":["Amberline Media","NO — stale/partial evidence","Historical E12 (2023) names VO-9800; sold Nov 2024 per E13","Advertising only — E15, 2025-06-01","Unresolved; A80 retained but maintenance not supplied (E14)","Historical E12 only; current access unresolved","Low: 2023 case study contradicted/qualified by 2025 equipment note","No current comparable rate; case study not a quote","=0  [缓存: 缺失]","8 weeks for 600 items in 2023 case study; not current/scale-comparable","Case study: 24-bit WAV, ProRes, EBUCore XML; current specs unknown","Named U-matic machine sold; 3.75 ips and DAT current access unresolved; “6–10 weeks” advertisement lacks batch basis","EXCLUDE — E12–E15"]},{"r":"11","cells":["Estimate basis — 1,400-tape mix"]},{"r":"12","cells":["Format / speed","Tapes","Thistledown quote (£/tape)","Extended (£)","Thistledown published (£/tape)","Extended (£)"]},{"r":"13","cells":["U-matic","400","24","=B13*C13  [缓存: 缺失]","22","=B13*E13  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"14","cells":["DAT","300","19","=B14*C14  [缓存: 缺失]","18","=B14*E14  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"15","cells":["1/4-inch open reel — 3.75 ips","350","30","=B15*C15  [缓存: 缺失]","28","=B15*E15  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"16","cells":["1/4-inch open reel — 7.5 ips","350","35","=B16*C16  [缓存: 缺失]","32","=B16*E16  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"17","cells":["TOTAL","=SUM(B13:B16)  [缓存: 缺失]","","=SUM(D13:D16)  [缓存: 缺失]","","=SUM(F13:F16)  [缓存: 缺失]"]},{"r":"19","cells":["Selected estimate: Thistledown quotation E06 = £38,050 (newer, scope-specific; published E05 comparison = £35,200). Formula is visible above."]},{"r":"20","cells":["Fallback method: where fresh tests/confirmations are unavailable, use the strongest dated evidence available as an interim panel basis; it does not prove performance on every tape or reserve capacity."]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Source index","row_count":10,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Source index and assessment conventions"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Label","Meaning / use"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Supported/current","Dated operational confirmation in packet; treated as current only at 30 June 2025."]},{"r":"5","cells":["Advertising only","Marketing statement without dated operational confirmation; recorded but not sufficient for full capability."]},{"r":"6","cells":["Historical","Older case study; not equivalent to current access, especially where equipment later sold."]},{"r":"7","cells":["Unresolved/contingent","Claim depends on sourcing, maintenance, partner, or missing detail; remains a risk."]},{"r":"8","cells":["E01–E21","Entry IDs map directly to rows in references/vendor_evidence_packet.xlsx."]},{"r":"9","cells":["Cost formula","Scope mix: 400 U-matic + 300 DAT + 350 reels at 3.75 ips + 350 reels at 7.5 ips = 1,400."]},{"r":"10","cells":["Estimate selection","Thistledown E06 quotation selected because it is newer and scope-specific; E05 published sheet retained for comparison."]},{"r":"11","cells":["Jurisdiction/date","England procurement context; evidence cut-off 30 June 2025; deadline 20 September 2025."]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/private/gold/digitisation_vendor_recommendation.docx","bytes":39135,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/8c27d92108a62cd3e4bda0d3c2d3bbddff761de910d951847e30ea50c6b7c0f6.docx","sha256":"8c27d92108a62cd3e4bda0d3c2d3bbddff761de910d951847e30ea50c6b7c0f6","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Tessington Heritage Archive\nDigitisation vendor recommendation\nProcurement panel pack | 20 September 2025 deadline | evidence cut-off 30 June 2025\nDecision: appoint Thistledown Studios.\nThe grant-funded collection is 1,400 tapes: 400 U-matic, 300 DAT, 350 1/4-inch open reel at 3.75 ips and 350 at 7.5 ips. Thistledown has detailed, dated operational confirmation for each required format and speed (E01–E04, 18 June 2025). That meets the same full-collection capability rule used in the comparison workbook; advertising, historical case-study and contingent claims are not treated as equivalent.\nWhy this is defensible\nPanel test\nEvidence-based finding\nCapability\nCurrent U-matic, DAT and both reel speeds are each confirmed in the 18 June operations email. Northmere also states all four, but without serials, test file or reserved capacity; it is an evidenced comparator, not the recommendation.\nCost\nThe newer, scope-specific 24 June quotation is used: 400×£24 + 300×£19 + 350×£30 + 350×£35 = £38,050. The 15 January published sheet totals £35,200; both figures remain visible in the workbook rather than being silently reconciled.\nTiming\nThistledown states 10 weeks for up to 1,500 tapes from receipt, condition dependent (E06), covering the 1,400-tape scope. This is a stated batch qualifier, not a converted per-item promise.\nDeliverables\nThe quotation specifies BWF WAV 24-bit/96 kHz, a 1080p H.264 access copy, CSV metadata and checksum manifest. These are more specific than Thornbury’s basic CSV/16-bit offer; Northmere’s FFV1/WAV/CSV is recorded for comparison.\nConfidence\nThe dated operations evidence is stronger than a web advertisement or the Amberline 2023 case study. Amberline’s named VO-9800 was sold in November 2024 (E13), so the case study cannot prove present U-matic access.\nShortlist tension and fallback. Ilse’s promise to include every bureau advertising all three formats is acknowledged by retaining Thornbury and Amberline in the comparison, but neither is presented as full-capability: Thornbury’s 7.5 ips evidence is advertising only, while Amberline’s equipment evidence is stale. Because fresh tests or confirmations cannot be obtained from every candidate before the panel, the defensible fallback is to use the strongest dated packet evidence as an interim decision basis. It limits confidence to what the documents establish; it does not prove every tape will play or reserve capacity.\nPrincipal residual risk. Thistledown’s £38,050 quotation conflicts with its £35,200 published sheet and excludes severe mould/baking and carrier return; its 10-week statement is condition dependent and no test transfer was supplied. The quotation is nevertheless the selected estimate because it is newer and expressly covers up to 1,500 tapes.\nRecommendation: appoint Thistledown Studios for the 1,400-tape collection at the estimated quotation basis of £38,050 and stated 10-week batch turnaround, subject to the documented evidence limits.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Both required deliverables exist at the top level with the exact requested filenames and readable file types.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Submitted working-directory files.","grader_hint":"Check exact names, extensions, and that both files open successfully."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recommendation document is no more than two rendered pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX pagination.","grader_hint":"Render with a standard office renderer and count pages."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook covers every candidate in the supplied packet and does not omit a candidate that meets the task's credible-capability definition.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook candidate list compared with the packet.","grader_hint":"Audit the packet's candidate universe and compare each candidate's treatment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A bureau is treated as capable of the full collection only when the evidence supports current handling of U-matic, DAT, and both specified 1/4-inch open-reel speeds.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Format and speed fields plus capability assessment.","grader_hint":"Check that no missing format or speed is silently treated as covered."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook explicitly distinguishes current operational evidence from advertising, historical case-study evidence, and unverified claims.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence-status labels and notes.","grader_hint":"Look for explicit source-status language, not merely source URLs or dates."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The 2023 case study is not used as sufficient current proof where the packet says the named machine was subsequently sold.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Case-study row, equipment-status note, and capability conclusion.","grader_hint":"Trace the affected vendor and confirm the stale evidence is qualified or excluded from current proof."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook shows both published-price and quotation figures where they conflict and explains the basis selected for any estimate.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Price comparison and estimate-basis fields.","grader_hint":"Reconcile the relevant packet entries; do not award this for showing only one number."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Estimated collection costs are calculated from the stated 1,400-tape scope and the applicable rate basis rather than from an unexplained lump sum.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook formulas or transparent arithmetic.","grader_hint":"Recalculate from displayed scope, rates, format assumptions, and stated exclusions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Format mix and speed requirements are reflected in cost or feasibility calculations wherever the packet provides differentiated rates or constraints.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Format-level calculations and notes.","grader_hint":"Check that the two open-reel speeds are not collapsed when the source distinguishes them."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Turnaround is stated with its unit, scope, and any condition or capacity qualifier supplied by the packet.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Turnaround fields and source notes.","grader_hint":"Reject bare numbers that conceal whether the period is per item, batch, or whole collection."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The comparison records relevant output and handover specifications, including the packet-supported file or metadata details needed to compare deliverables.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Deliverable-specification columns and notes.","grader_hint":"Compare what each bureau actually supplies, not just whether digitisation is offered."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Evidence dates are shown and the assessment distinguishes current evidence as of 30 June 2025 from older material.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Dated evidence fields.","grader_hint":"Inspect dates against source entries and the stated as-of date."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook identifies unresolved capability, price, capacity, or deliverable risks instead of converting missing evidence into a positive assertion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Risk and unresolved-question fields.","grader_hint":"Sample gaps and verify they remain visibly qualified."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Inclusion and exclusion decisions are supported by cited packet evidence rather than by unsupported reputation or invented market facts.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence references beside decisions.","grader_hint":"Trace each decision to a packet row, quotation, dated statement, or explicit absence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The workbook is usable as an auditable panel comparison: a reviewer can follow each material conclusion back to a source entry and calculation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Overall workbook inspection.","grader_hint":"Judge traceability, legibility, and whether a procurement reviewer could challenge or reproduce the conclusions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recommendation document names exactly one recommended bureau.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation statement in the DOCX.","grader_hint":"Count recommendation calls; alternatives may be discussed but must not be presented as co-recommendations."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recommended bureau satisfies the same full-format capability standard used in the workbook.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Memo recommendation cross-checked with workbook capability assessment.","grader_hint":"A vendor recommended despite unsupported current capability fails this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recommendation weighs capability, cost, turnaround, deliverables, and evidence confidence rather than relying on a single attractive attribute.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Memo rationale.","grader_hint":"Require substantive treatment of all five decision dimensions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo states the 1,400-tape scope and its cost estimate agrees with the workbook's selected estimate basis.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Shared figures in both deliverables.","grader_hint":"Recalculate the workbook estimate and compare the memo figure within ±$1 or the source currency's equivalent rounding."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo's turnaround figure and scope agree with the workbook, including units and material qualifiers.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Shared turnaround statements.","grader_hint":"Do not accept a memo number that silently changes batch scope or conditions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo explains why the stale 2023 equipment evidence does not by itself establish present capability.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Memo discussion of dated equipment evidence.","grader_hint":"Look for the sold-machine issue and its effect on confidence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo explains how the conflicting price sheet and quotation were handled.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Memo pricing rationale.","grader_hint":"The explanation must identify the conflict and the estimate basis."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recommendation acknowledges the tension between Ilse's promised comprehensive shortlist and the need not to claim unsupported capability.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Memo framing and rationale.","grader_hint":"Require a defensible treatment of the promise, not merely a mention of it."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo presents a defensible fallback for the inability to obtain test transfers or fresh confirmations from every candidate and states its limitation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Memo risk or fallback discussion.","grader_hint":"Look for an evidence-based interim decision approach with an explicit boundary on what it proves."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo does not present invented rates, equipment, capacity, insurance, accreditation, or contractual terms as facts.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Claims in the DOCX compared with the packet.","grader_hint":"Check every material assertion against the supplied source and its uncertainty."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo identifies the principal residual risk or evidence limitation associated with the single recommendation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Memo risk statement.","grader_hint":"A generic statement that all procurement has risk is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memo is concise, decision-ready, and understandable to a procurement panel rather than written as engineering notes.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX inspection.","grader_hint":"Judge audience fit, sequencing, clarity, and whether the recommendation can be located and acted upon."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo ends on the single decision and does not conclude with a list of next steps.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final paragraph of the DOCX.","grader_hint":"A risk qualification may precede the decision; the ending must not become an action plan."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The two deliverables agree on vendor names, capability conclusions, selected price basis, total estimate, and turnaround wherever those facts are shared.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-deliverable audit.","grader_hint":"Compare the memo against the workbook and flag contradictions, not harmless additional detail."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook and memo preserve the distinction between what the packet establishes and what remains unknown.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Both deliverables' labels and prose.","grader_hint":"Award only when uncertainty is consistently represented rather than buried in a disclaimer."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"You are an audio and video technician supporting Tessington Heritage Archive's procurement panel. You must turn a supplied evidence packet into a defensible vendor comparison and a single recommendation for an external-facing archival digitisation decision.","difficulty_sources":["material ambiguity about what counts as a genuinely current capability","reconciliation of conflicting evidence and commercial figures","a promised comprehensive shortlist that may conflict with defensible evidence standards","a deadline that prevents the textbook approach of obtaining test transfers from every candidate"],"authoring_plan":{"source_file":{"filename":"vendor_evidence_packet.xlsx","purpose":"Create one compact synthetic evidence packet containing all facts needed to derive the comparison and recommendation offline.","content_constraints":["Use only synthetic vendor and contact details; no real addresses, account numbers, or personal identifiers.","Include Thistledown Studios and Thornbury Health Network as named candidate organisations, plus additional synthetic candidate bureaus as needed to create a meaningful feasible set.","Include candidate evidence for U-matic, DAT, and 1/4-inch open reel at the two required speeds, with a mixture of current operational confirmations, marketing claims, unresolved claims, and an excluded candidate missing at least one required capability.","Include a 2023 case study naming a machine that a later dated note says the vendor sold, so the case study cannot establish current capability by itself.","Include a published price sheet and a conflicting quotation for at least one viable candidate, with enough rate detail to calculate the 1,400-tape collection estimate by format and speed.","Include turnaround statements, capacity qualifiers, output formats, metadata or handover specifications, and any material limitations needed for comparison.","Make every source entry internally consistent and dateable as of 30 June 2025; do not require internet lookup.","Provide enough format counts or a stated collection mix to permit a transparent total-cost calculation for 1,400 tapes without making the solver guess."]},"gold_derivation":{"capability_rule":"A full-collection candidate must have current, credible evidence for all three required format families and both open-reel speeds. Historical or advertising evidence may be recorded but cannot be treated as equivalent to current operational confirmation when contradicted or weakened by later equipment-status evidence.","pricing_rule":"The gold comparison retains both conflicting commercial figures, identifies the selected estimate basis, and calculates the collection total from the supplied format mix and 1,400-tape scope. The memo repeats that selected total and its basis.","turnaround_rule":"Use the packet's stated unit and qualifiers; do not convert a per-item or batch statement into a whole-collection promise unless the packet supports that calculation.","recommendation_rule":"The intended recommendation is the single candidate that is both currently credible across the complete format set and defensible on combined capability, cost, timing, deliverable fit, and evidence confidence. It need not be the cheapest candidate.","uncertainty_rule":"Missing confirmation, stale equipment evidence, contradictory rates, and capacity limitations remain visible as uncertainty or risk rather than being filled with invented facts.","fallback_rule":"The gold memo acknowledges that fresh tests or confirmations cannot be obtained from every candidate before the panel and uses the strongest available dated evidence as an interim basis while clearly limiting what that evidence proves.","cross_file_rule":"The workbook and memo must share one vendor recommendation, one scope, one selected total-cost figure, and one turnaround statement."}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"primary_plus_appendix","structure":"required_sections"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"vendor_evidence_packet","filename":"vendor_evidence_packet.xlsx","purpose":"The sole offline evidence source for supplier identities, format and speed claims, dated operational confirmations, published prices, conflicting quote information, equipment-status notes, turnaround statements, and deliverable specifications.","required":true,"discovery":"The file is supplied in the working directory and is named exactly `vendor_evidence_packet.xlsx`."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"comparison_workbook","filename":"digitisation_vendor_comparison.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"An auditable comparison of all credible candidate bureaus and the evidence-supported reasons for inclusion or exclusion.","required":true,"constraints":["Must be saved at the top level of the working directory with exactly this filename.","Must include traceable calculations for the 1,400-tape scope.","Must distinguish supported facts, supplier claims, conflicts, assumptions, and unresolved risks.","Must be readable without relying on hidden cells or external links."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"recommendation_memo","filename":"digitisation_vendor_recommendation.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A concise procurement-panel recommendation that makes one clear vendor call and explains the evidence, cost, timing, deliverables, and risk.","required":true,"constraints":["Must be saved at the top level of the working directory with exactly this filename.","Must be no more than two pages when rendered.","Must state exactly one recommended bureau.","Must agree with the workbook on every shared figure, especially scope, estimated total cost, and turnaround.","Must end with the decision rather than a list of next steps."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"document_information","work_product":"media_edit","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"audio_video_technicians","sector":"information","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":8.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Have a domain-experienced reviewer validate the capability judgments and a separate document-quality reviewer verify calculations, cross-file agreement, page limit, and decision usability.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The supplied evidence packet is a synthetic offline snapshot, so the task assesses evidence handling and professional decision quality rather than live market completeness.","Currency and vendor-specific facts must be taken from the packet; graders should allow transparent rounding consistent with the source."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:47:52+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:47:52+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:47:52+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:47:52+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R25']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:47:52+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/9356628262df0852","declared_deliverables":["digitisation_vendor_comparison.xlsx","digitisation_vendor_recommendation.docx"]};
